    "tree": {
      "sha": "0154f4f901483413fc715308cdb6568153393d53",
      "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/MohamedRejeb/Calf/git/trees/0154f4f901483413fc715308cdb6568153393d53"
    },
    "message": "chore(deps): bump Kotlin 2.4.20, Compose 1.12.0, AGP 9.4.0, compileSdk 37 for 0.14.0\n\n- Kotlin 2.4.10 -> 2.4.20, Compose Multiplatform 1.11.1 -> 1.12.0 with its\n  paired Material3 1.12.0-alpha03 and JetBrains Navigation 2.10.0-alpha02\n- AGP 8.13.2 -> 9.4.0, compileSdk 36 -> 37, Gradle 9.0.0 -> 9.7.1\n- Migrate every library module to com.android.kotlin.multiplatform.library:\n  AGP 9 no longer allows com.android.library + kotlin.multiplatform in one\n  subproject. The hierarchy template matches the AGP target explicitly\n  because KGP's withAndroidTarget() only matches its own androidTarget(),\n  which silently dropped materialMain from the Android compilation\n- sample:android uses AGP's built-in Kotlin and moves to minSdk 24 because\n  JetBrains navigation 2.10 requires it; calf-navigation keeps androidx\n  navigation 2.9.7 so the library stays at minSdk 23\n- Web targets: only modules with browser-run tests bundle test executables\n  (CMP-4906); the CMP check is skipped for targets without test sources\n- CI runs on macos-26: CMP 1.11+ needs Xcode 26 to link ui-uikit, which is\n  why main is red on macos-14\n- Drop deprecated gradle.properties flags and `by registering` task DSL\n- kotlinx-datetime 0.8.0, Coil 3.6.2, Ktor 3.5.2, Vanniktech 0.37.0,\n  kyant backdrop 2.0.1 / shapes 1.2.1, appcompat 1.8.0, androidx compose 1.12.1\n- Document that Compose 1.12 requires compileSdk 37 for Android consumers",
